# Li - Ugur interatomic potential, switched, with the angular factor
#
# pair_style ugur/ang
# pair_coeff * * Li_taper.ugur.ang Li
#
# Truncation: switched from 0.85 of each cutoff to the cutoff, quintic, C2 - energy is conserved in MD: measured drift 0.4 meV/atom/ns for copper, 876x less than its hard twin.  USE for molecular dynamics, which no hard set can do.  It pays for that on the dispersion: the switched sets average 12.7 % against the hard sets' 9.5 %, because switching the pair term off over the outer 15 % moves the force constants at the largest separations, which is the short-wavelength end, and nothing in the fit sees it
# MD: DO NOT USE.  At 600 K this structure disintegrates - 432 atoms become 13 and LAMMPS stops.
#
# Lattice stability: screened on the 8^3 and 9^3 meshes AND along the
# symmetry path; no imaginary modes.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Li at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
